@startuml Project01_Activity_Butterfly
title Butterfly — what it does every cycle

start
:A butterfly wakes up for this cycle;

:Flutter around randomly;

if (Is it time to try reproducing?) then (yes)
  :Look for another butterfly nearby;
  if (Found a partner?) then (yes)
    :Each parent passes on\none of its colors;
    note right
      A black butterfly always passes on black.
      A white butterfly always passes on white.
      A gray butterfly passes on
      black or white, at random.
    end note
    :Combine both colors\nto decide the baby's color;
    note right
      Two blacks -> black baby
      Two whites -> white baby
      One of each -> gray baby
    end note
    :A new baby butterfly is born\nnext to its parent;
  else (no)
    :No partner found, skip reproducing;
  endif
else (no)
endif

if (Does it die of old age / natural causes\nthis cycle?) then (yes)
  :The butterfly dies;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Butterfly survives to the next cycle;
stop

@enduml
